        "comments": "The assembly drSaxCesp1.hap1.1 is based on 72x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial and plastid genomes were assembled using OATK. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. There are four different HiC patterns on the map, suggesting the species is a hybrid of 4 species. It could have been a allotetraploid, but today works as a functional diploid (2n = 78). The HAP1 file contains one copy of each subgenome.",
